---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalLayout from '@components/article/LegalLayout.astro';
import { buildCategorySchema, buildMeta } from '@lib/seo';

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: 'Affiliate disclaimer',
  description:
    'SleekDrops earns a commission when you click affiliate links. We research every pick independently, never accept paid placements, and disclose every commercial relationship.',
  pathname: '/disclaimer',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  {...meta}
  schema={buildCategorySchema('Affiliate disclaimer', '/disclaimer', meta.description)}
  screen="disclaimer"
>
  <LegalLayout
    eyebrow="Legal"
    titleHtml="Affiliate <em>disclaimer</em>."
    updated="September 6, 2026"
    toc={[
      { href: '#summary',    label: 'Plain summary' },
      { href: '#how',        label: 'How affiliate links work' },
      { href: '#independence', label: 'Editorial independence' },
      { href: '#testing',    label: 'How we research' },
      { href: '#labelling',  label: 'How links are labelled' },
      { href: '#corrections', label: 'Corrections' },
    ]}
  >
    <div class="summary" id="summary">
      <strong>Plain summary</strong>
      Most product links on SleekDrops are affiliate links. We earn a small commission if you buy — at no extra cost to you. Editorial choices come first; the link is what we do after we've decided what to recommend.
    </div>

    <h2 id="how">How affiliate links <em>work</em></h2>
    <p>When you click a product link on SleekDrops, you're sent to the retailer (Amazon, Best Buy, the brand directly, and so on). If you make a qualifying purchase within their cookie window, the retailer attributes the sale to SleekDrops and pays us a small commission. The price you pay is the same — the retailer absorbs the commission out of their margin, not your wallet.</p>

    <h2 id="independence">Editorial <em>independence</em></h2>
    <p>We don't take sponsorships. We don't run "promoted" or "sponsored" posts. No brand or PR agency pays us to publish, and no brand has approval or pre-view rights over a SleekDrops review. The recommendation comes first; the affiliate link is bolted on after we've decided what to recommend.</p>
    <p>No brand has supplied us with a product. If one ever does, the piece will say so, and we will return the unit or disclose ongoing access in the byline.</p>

    <h2 id="testing">How we <em>research</em></h2>
    <p>We research; we do not lab-test every product, and we don't claim to. Here is what a recommendation rests on:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Reviews</strong> compare a product against its nearest competitors on manufacturer specifications, owner reviews and expert coverage, with Australian availability checked on the date the piece shows.</li>
      <li><strong>Buying guides</strong> compare at least three contenders side by side on the same criteria.</li>
      <li><strong>Roundups</strong> are ranked against stated criteria — we'll always tell you what we weighted and why.</li>
      <li><strong>Hands-on use</strong> is called out where it exists. Where a pick rests on research rather than our own use, the piece says so.</li>
      <li><strong>Pros and cons</strong> are honest: 3–5 genuine advantages, 2–4 genuine disadvantages. If we can't find any cons, we haven't looked hard enough yet.</li>
      <li><strong>Prices</strong> are not quoted from Amazon. Amazon's programme only allows prices drawn live from its own systems, so we point you to the current price instead; where a figure matters we give the manufacturer's RRP with its year.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="labelling">How links are <em>labelled</em></h2>
    <p>Every affiliate link carries <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the HTML, per Google's guidance, and every page with one opens with a disclosure under the byline. Buttons and links that say "Check price on Amazon", "See it on Amazon" or similar are always affiliate and always go to Amazon; in-body text links to manufacturers, standards bodies and other sources are not.</p>

    <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
    <p>Spotted a mistake — a stale price, an old promo code, or a claim that no longer holds? Tell us at <a href="mailto:corrections@sleekdrops.com">corrections@sleekdrops.com</a> and we'll update the post (and credit you in the footer if you'd like).</p>
  </LegalLayout>
</BaseLayout>
